onitor              Caregiver Interface\n791:In Auto Control [==\n830:(CB_alarm_cufflnvalid! = false                                 CB_backManual = true\n845:Figure 5: Cuff Handler\n850:valid 1” to “In Auto Control”, specifically the statement “CB_backManual =\n851:true” which triggers the Algorithm component to return to Manual mode.\n897:28 If CARA can not obtain a valid blood pressure in 3 minutes, it should revert back to manual mode.\n907:44.3.1.3 The system will revert to manual mode\n912:Figure 6: Requirements for the Cuff Handler in Auto Control\n919:CA_Mode                CARA’s current mode                        Algorithm\n920:CB-alarm_cuffInvalid1 Level 1 Alarm                               Cuff Handler\n921:CB-alarm_cuffInvalid2 Level 2 Alarm                                Cuff Handler\n922:CB_backManual          Go back to manual mode                       Cuff Handler\n925:CB-_cuffFrequency       Frequency to read Control BP (seconds)      Cuff Handler\n929:CB_iterations            Number of iterations                          Cuff Handler\n930:CB_localTimer           Local Timer                                     Cuff Handler\n932:Figure 7: Variables of the Cuff Handler EFSM\n1256:Mode_Control_Algorithm\n1303:Mode_Control_Algorithm mode and the Polling_Algorithm mode. Figure 11\n1304:describes the Mode_Control_Algorithm mode. In the Mode_Control_Algorithm\n1310:mode, we specify the four states of CARA - wait, manual, autocontrol init, and\n1311:autocontrol — and the Ask_StartAC submode. While the transition labels are\n1322:sition labels of EFSM. In the Ask_StartAC submode, the setpoint value can be\n1323:changed and AutocontrolInit may be entered by pushing the StartAC button.\n1341:Figure 11: Mode_Control_Algorithm mode\n1357:Mode_Control_Algorithm mode, we always have CA_Mode = Manual. A mode\n1362:e (CA_Mode = Manual) at Manual_Mode point of the Mode_Control_Algorithm\n1460:e CA_Mode # AUTO\n1473:e CB_backManual = false\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
